# Tutorial 3a, read after tutorial 3's .env (HOST_IP and the OpenMCX images stay there). A variable set in the shell
# wins over both, e.g. GNB_OPTS= ./qos.sh up.
#
# The openMCX QoS RAN and core from Docker Hub (github.com/openMCX/oai): the gNB, the nr-UE, the AMF, SMF and UPF.
# Built yourself with its tools/build.sh: oai-<nf>:mcx-qos.
# The PCF and the other core functions stay tutorial 3's.
GNB_IMG=openmcx/oai-gnb:mcx-qos
NRUE_IMG=openmcx/oai-nr-ue:mcx-qos
AMF_IMG=openmcx/oai-amf:mcx-qos
SMF_IMG=openmcx/oai-smf:mcx-qos
UPF_IMG=openmcx/oai-upf:mcx-qos
# The MC clients in the UEs: openmcx-client's main branch from 2026-10-28 or later (mcvideo.live, the video at a set
# rate); openmcx/openmcx-client:develop is older.
CLIENT_IMG=openmcx/openmcx-client:mcx-qos
#
# The small cell of the walk-through: the gNB's MCS capped at 4 in both directions (about 7 Mbit/s UL). Empty: the
# full 106-PRB cell.
GNB_OPTS=--MACRLCs.[0].dl_max_mcs 4 --MACRLCs.[0].ul_max_mcs 4
# GBR admission: the share of the cell's PRBs per direction that GBR flows may take, e.g. 0.9; empty: off.
OAI_MCX_GBR_ADMISSION=
# 1: voice in RLC UM with a discard timer of twice the PDB; empty: RLC AM, as stock OAI.
OAI_MCX_RLC_UM=
# The UE pools whose N6 downlink the UPF serves before best effort (the DNN mcptt); GBR flows go first anyway.
OAI_MCX_UPF_PRIORITY_SUBNETS=12.1.1.0/24
#
# MCVideo: the video's rate (the GFBR asked for is 10 % above), picture size and key frame interval
VIDEO_KBPS=4096
VIDEO_SIZE=640x480
VIDEO_KEY_INTERVAL=30
